USER Can I have runtime assertions in rust?
-------
ASSISTANT Yes, Rust has several ways to do runtime assertions:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 1. **`assert!` macro** - Basic assertion:
ASSISTANT    ```rust
ASSISTANT    assert!(condition, "Optional error message");
ASSISTANT    ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 2. **`assert_eq!` / `assert_ne!`** - For equality checks:
ASSISTANT    ```rust
ASSISTANT    assert_eq!(left, right, "Optional message");
ASSISTANT    assert_ne!(left, right);
ASSISTANT    ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 3. **`debug_assert!`** - Only active in debug builds:
ASSISTANT    ```rust
ASSISTANT    debug_assert!(condition);
ASSISTANT    ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 4. **`panic!`** - Explicitly fail with a message:
ASSISTANT    ```rust
ASSISTANT    panic!("This should never happen");
ASSISTANT    ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 5. **Custom assertions** - You can create your own:
ASSISTANT    ```rust
ASSISTANT    if !condition {
ASSISTANT        eprintln!("Assertion failed: {}", message);
ASSISTANT        std::process::exit(1);
ASSISTANT    }
ASSISTANT    ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT All of these will:
ASSISTANT - Do nothing if the condition is true
ASSISTANT - Panic (terminate the program) if the condition is false
ASSISTANT - Can include custom error messages
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Would you like me to show how to use any of these in your specific code?
