USER How can I encode a Vec as a base64 string in rust?
USER 
USER Reply in English.
LLM RESPONSE 2026-06-08T22:48:11
ASSISTANT You can use the `base64` crate to encode a `Vec<u8>` as a base64 string in Rust. Here's an example:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```rust
ASSISTANT use base64::Engine as _; // Import the Engine trait
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT fn encode_vec_to_base64(vec: &Vec<u8>) -> String {
ASSISTANT     base64::engine::general_purpose::STANDARD.encode(vec)
ASSISTANT }
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT This uses the standard base64 alphabet with padding. If you need a different configuration (e.g., URL-safe base64 without padding), you can use a different engine like `URL_SAFE_NO_PAD`.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT To use this, you'll need to add the `base64` crate to your `Cargo.toml`:
ASSISTANT ```toml
ASSISTANT [dependencies]
ASSISTANT base64 = "0.21"
ASSISTANT ```
